          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.12,
            0.884,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find equivalent fractions for the given pairs of fractions such that the fractional units are the same. a. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 7 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " b. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{8}{3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{5}{6}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " c. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{4}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{3}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " d. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 6 } { 7 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{8}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " e. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 9 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " f. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 1 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{2}{9}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " g. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{8}{3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " h. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 3 } { 6 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 9 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.264,
            0.884,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Expressing a fraction in lowest terms (or in its simplest form)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.315,
            0.884,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In any fraction, if its numerator and denominator have no common factor except 1, then the fraction is said to be in "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "lowest terms",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm { 0 r }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in its "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "simplest form",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". In other words, a fraction is said to be in lowest terms if its numerator and denominator are as small as possible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.406,
            0.884,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Any fraction can be expressed in lowest terms by finding an equivalent fraction whose numerator and denominator are as small as possible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.194,
            0.474,
            0.726,
            0.496
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let’s see how to express fractions in lowest terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.503,
            0.884,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ": Is the fraction "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{16}{20}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in lowest terms? No, 4 is a common factor of 16 and 20. Let us reduce "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 6 } { 2 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to lowest terms."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.559,
            0.884,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We know that both 16 (numerator) and 20 (denominator) are divisible by 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.613,
            0.305,
            0.642
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{16 \\div 4}{20 \\div 4} \\; = \\frac{4}{5}."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.645,
            0.883,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, there is no common factor between 4 and 5. Hence, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 6 } { 2 0 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " expressed in lowest terms is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 4 } { 5 } } ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{4}{5}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is called the simplest form of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 1 6 } { 2 0 } } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " since 4 and 5 have no common factor other than 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.269,
            0.77,
            0.561,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Any fraction can be converted to lowest terms by dividing both the numerator and denominator by the highest common factor between them."
            }
          ]
        },
